PART 5: S3 (Simple Storage Service)

Interview Importance: ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ (Very High)

Amazon S3 (Simple Storage Service) is AWS's highly scalable object storage service. It is designed to store and retrieve virtually unlimited amounts of data with high durability and availability.

For DevOps engineers, S3 is commonly used for:

Application backups
Jenkins build artifacts
Static website hosting
Log storage
Terraform remote state
CloudFront origin
Data lakes
What is S3?

S3 is an object storage service.

Unlike EBS, S3 does not store data as disks or filesystems.

Instead, it stores:

Object = File + Metadata + Unique Key

Example:

Bucket

photos/

      image1.jpg

      image2.jpg

      image3.jpg
