Storage Classes

Choosing the right storage class is a common interview topic.

1. S3 Standard

Best for:

Frequently accessed files
Websites
Mobile apps

Features:

Low latency
High availability
2. S3 Intelligent-Tiering

AWS automatically moves objects between access tiers based on usage.

Good when access patterns are unpredictable.

3. S3 Standard-IA (Infrequent Access)

Suitable for:

Backups
Disaster recovery

Lower storage cost, but retrieval incurs a fee.

4. S3 One Zone-IA

Stores data in a single Availability Zone.

Suitable for:

Re-creatable data
Secondary backups

Lower cost but less resilient than multi-AZ storage.

5. S3 Glacier Instant Retrieval

Used for archives that still require quick access.

6. S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval

Used for long-term backups where retrieval can take minutes or hours.

7. S3 Glacier Deep Archive

Cheapest storage option.

Suitable for:

Compliance
Long-term archival (years)

Retrieval may take many hours.

